```text
Connor White, Planning & Development Department, provided a staffreport. Committee members
Rinne and Segrave commented on the item.
11.
ORDINANCE —3”’ READING
Amending the Official Zoning Map of the City of
Cheyenne establishing the zoning classification of MUR Mixed-Use Residential for land
annexed to the City of Cheyenne located east of US-30 and north of and adjacent to East
Pershing Boulevard.
Mr. Segrave moved to approve on 3”’ and final reading, seconded by Dr. Rinne. Motion carried
by unanimous voice vote.
Connor White, Planning & Development Department, provided a staff report.
12.
ORDINANCE —3”’ READING
— Amending the Official Zoning Map of the City of
Cheyenne changing the zoning classification from LI Light Industrial to CB Community
Business for land located northeast of the intersection of Hutchins Drive and Industry
Drive.
Dr. Riime moved to approve on 3”’ and final reading, seconded by Mr. Segrave. Motion carried
by unanimous voice vote.
Connor White, Planning & Development Department, provided a staff report and Seth Lloyd,
Planning & Development Department, provided additional information.
Chairman Roybal and
committee member Rinne commented on the item.
14.
ORDINANCE —3”’ READING
— Amending Section 2.76.040, Designation of Downtown
Development District, of Chapter 2.76, Downtown Development Authority, of Title 2,
Administration and Personnel, of the Municipal Code of the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming,
to expand the Downtown Development District.
Dr. Rinne moved to approve on 3”’ and final reading, seconded by Mr. Segrave. Motion carried by
unanimous voice vote.
Kylie Dorr, Downtown Development Authority Administrator, provided a staff report.
16.
RESOLUTION
— Approving sanitary sewer service, by Outside User Agreement, for Oh
Hail No LLC, for land located south of Robert Avenue and west of South Greeley
Highway. (SPONSOR - MR. ROYBAL)
Dr. Rinne moved to adopt, seconded by Mr. Laybourn. Dr. Rinne moved to amend by substitute
dated August 30, 2024, seconded by Mr. Laybourn. Motion to amend carried by unanimous voice
vote. Main motion, as amended, carried with Mr. Laybourn and Dr. Rinne voting “YES” and Mr.
Segrave voting “NO.”
Connor White, Planning & Development Department, provided a staff report and introduced a
proposed substitute. Seth Lloyd, Planning & Development Department, and Frank Strong, Board
